    "title": "if",
    "pageid": 8376,
    "revid": 93526786,
    "text": "<div class=\"mw-parser-output\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"English\">English</h2></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Etymology\">Etymology</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Pronunciation\">Pronunciation</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Conjunction\">Conjunction</h3></div>\n<ol><li><a href=\"/wiki/supposing\" title=\"supposing\">Supposing</a> that, <a href=\"/wiki/assuming\" title=\"assuming\">assuming</a> that, in the <a href=\"/wiki/circumstance\" title=\"circumstance\">circumstances</a> that; <span class=\"use-with-mention\">suppositive used to introduce a <a href=\"/wiki/condition#English\" title=\"condition\">condition</a> that may be (or prove to be) either true or false.</span>\n\n<ol><li><span class=\"usage-label-sense\"><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">(</span><span class=\"ib-content label-content\"><a href=\"/wiki/computing#Noun\" title=\"computing\">computing</a></span><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">)</span></span> A keyword that invokes conditional processing: in the event that a given condition is true, execute the given statement(s) (otherwise execute other statements).\n</li></ol></li>\n<li>Supposing that; <span class=\"use-with-mention\">used with past or past perfect subjunctive to indicate a <a href=\"/wiki/counterfactual#English\" title=\"counterfactual\">counterfactual</a> or <a href=\"/wiki/hypothetical#English\" title=\"hypothetical\">hypothetical</a> condition.</span>\n\n<ol><li><span class=\"usage-label-sense\"><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">(</span><span class=\"ib-content label-content\">usually <a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#hyperbolic\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">hyperbolic</a></span><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">)</span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/even\" title=\"even\">Even</a> if; even in the circumstances that.\n\n<ul><li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>1838</b></span>, Boz [pseudonym; <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Dickens\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Charles Dickens\">Charles Dickens</a>], <cite><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oliver_Twist\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Oliver Twist\">Oliver Twist;<span class=\"q-hellip-sp\">&#160;</span><span class=\"q-hellip-b\"><span style=\"font-style: normal;\">[</span></span><span title=\"or, The Parish Boy’s Progress. By “Boz.” In Three Volumes.\">…</span><span class=\"q-hellip-b\"><span style=\"font-style: normal;\">]</span></span><span class=\"q-hellip-b\"></span></a></cite>, volume , London: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Bentley_(publisher)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Richard Bentley (publisher)\">Richard Bentley</a>,<span class=\"q-hellip-sp\">&#160;</span><span class=\"q-hellip-b\"><span style=\"font-style: normal;\">[</span></span><span title=\"New Burlington Street\">…</span><span class=\"q-hellip-b\"><span style=\"font-style: normal;\">]</span></span><span class=\"q-hellip-b\"></span>, <small><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://search.worldcat.org/title/558204586\">→OCLC</a></small>:</span></div></li>\n<li><b>2004</b>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Lee_Murphy\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:David Lee Murphy\">David Lee Murphy</a> and Kim Tribble (writers), <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montgomery_Gentry\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Montgomery Gentry\">Montgomery Gentry</a> (singers), “<b>If</b> It’s The Last Thing I Do” (song), in <i>You Do Your Thing</i> (album):\n</li></ul></li></ol></li>\n<li>Considering the fact that; <a href=\"/wiki/given_that\" title=\"given that\">given that</a>; <span class=\"use-with-mention\">introducing a condition that is known to be true</span>.\n\n<ul><li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>1596</b></span>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edmund_Spenser\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Edmund Spenser\">Edmund Spenser</a>, “Book I”, in <cite><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Faerie_Queene\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:The Faerie Queene\">The Faerie Queene.<span class=\"q-hellip-sp\">&#160;</span><span class=\"q-hellip-b\"><span style=\"font-style: normal;\">[</span></span><span title=\"Disposed into Twelue Bookes, Fashioning XII. Morall Vertues.\">…</span><span class=\"q-hellip-b\"><span style=\"font-style: normal;\">]</span></span><span class=\"q-hellip-b\"></span></a></cite>, part I (books I–III), London: <span class=\"q-hellip-sp\"> </span><span class=\"q-hellip-b\"><span style=\"font-style: normal;\">[</span></span><span title=\"Printed [by]\">…</span><span class=\"q-hellip-b\"><span style=\"font-style: normal;\">]</span></span><span class=\"q-hellip-b\"> </span> [<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Field_(printer)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Richard Field (printer)\">Richard Field</a>] for <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Ponsonby_(publisher)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:William Ponsonby (publisher)\">William Ponsonbie</a>, <small><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://search.worldcat.org/title/932900760\">→OCLC</a></small>, stanza ii, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://archive.org/details/faeriequeenedisp01spen/page/66/mode/1up\">page <span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\">66</span></a>:</span></div></li></ul></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/when\" title=\"when\">When</a>; <a href=\"/wiki/whenever\" title=\"whenever\">whenever</a>; every time that.\n</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/although\" title=\"although\">Although</a>; <span class=\"use-with-mention\">used to introduce a concession</span>; may..but.\n\n<ul><li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><b>1981</b> April 11, Mitzel, “Kopacz Acquitted In Barbre Killing”, in <cite>Gay Community News</cite>, page 1:</span></div></li></ul></li>\n<li><span class=\"usage-label-sense\"><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">(</span><span class=\"ib-content label-content\"><a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#literary\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">literary</a></span><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">)</span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/while\" title=\"while\">While</a>; <span class=\"use-with-mention\">used to introduce a contrast</span>.\n\n<ul><li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><b>1957</b> March 7, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vladimir_Nabokov\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Vladimir Nabokov\">Vladimir Nabokov</a>, chapter 3.3, in <cite><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pnin_(novel)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Pnin (novel)\">Pnin</a></cite>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heinemann_(publisher)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Heinemann (publisher)\">Heinemann</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://archive.org/details/pnin0000nabo/page/66/mode/1up\">page <span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\">66</span></a>:</span></div></li>\n<li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>2015</b></span>, Phillips Payson O'Brien, <cite>How the War was Won: Air-Sea Power and Allied Victory in World War II</cite>, page <span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.google.com/books/edition/How_the_War_Was_Won/9hh2BgAAQBAJ?&gbpv=1&pg=PA8\">8</a></span>:</span></div></li>\n<li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>2015</b></span>, Phillips Payson O'Brien, <cite>How the War was Won: Air-Sea Power and Allied Victory in World War II</cite>, page <span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.google.com/books/edition/How_the_War_Was_Won/9hh2BgAAQBAJ?&gbpv=1&pg=PA65\">65</a></span>:</span></div></li>\n<li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>2015</b></span>, Phillips Payson O'Brien, <cite>How the War was Won: Air-Sea Power and Allied Victory in World War II</cite>, page <span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.google.com/books/edition/How_the_War_Was_Won/9hh2BgAAQBAJ?&gbpv=1&pg=PA103\">103</a></span>:</span></div></li>\n<li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>2023</b></span>, Serhii Plokhy, <cite>The Russo-Ukrainian War: The Return of History</cite>, page <span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.google.com/books/edition/The_Russo_Ukrainian_War/e3eoEAAAQBAJ?&gbpv=1&pg=PT17\">17</a></span>:</span></div></li>\n<li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>2023</b></span>, Serhii Plokhy, <cite>The Russo-Ukrainian War: The Return of History</cite>, page <span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.google.com/books/edition/The_Russo_Ukrainian_War/H2F_EAAAQBAJ?&gbpv=1&pg=PA1970\">1970</a></span>:</span></div></li>\n<li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>2023</b></span>, Serhii Plokhy, <cite>The Russo-Ukrainian War: The Return of History</cite>, page <span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.google.com/books/edition/The_Russo_Ukrainian_War/H2F_EAAAQBAJ?&gbpv=1&pg=PA1971\">1971</a></span>:</span></div></li></ul></li>\n<li><span class=\"usage-label-sense\"><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">(</span><span class=\"ib-content label-content\">sometimes <a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#proscribed\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">proscribed</a></span><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">)</span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/whether\" title=\"whether\">Whether</a>; <span class=\"use-with-mention\">used to introduce a noun clause, an indirect question, that functions as the direct object of certain verbs.</span>\n\n<ul><li><b>1715–1717</b>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matthew_Prior\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Matthew Prior\">Matthew Prior</a>, <i>Alma; or, The Progress of the Mind</i>, Canto III:\n</li>\n<li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>1976</b></span>, Michael Harrison, <cite>Beyond Baker Street: A Sherlockian Anthology</cite>, page <span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\">117</span>:</span></div></li></ul></li>\n<li><span class=\"use-with-mention\">Introducing a <a href=\"/wiki/relevance_conditional#English\" title=\"relevance conditional\">relevance conditional</a></span>; in case.\n</li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Usage_notes\">Usage notes</h4></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Alternative_forms\">Alternative forms</h4></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Derived_terms\">Derived terms</h4></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Translations\">Translations</h4></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Noun\">Noun</h3></div>\n<ol><li><span class=\"usage-label-sense\"><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">(</span><span class=\"ib-content label-content\"><a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#informal\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">informal</a></span><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">)</span></span> An <a href=\"/wiki/uncertainty\" title=\"uncertainty\">uncertainty</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/possibility\" title=\"possibility\">possibility</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/condition\" title=\"condition\">condition</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/doubt\" title=\"doubt\">doubt</a> etc.\n\n<ul><li><b>1709,</b> Susannah Centlivre, <i>The Busy Body</i>, Act III, in John Bell (ed.), <i>British Theater</i>, J. Bell (1791), <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://books.google.com/books?id=qYY0AAAAMAAJ&pg=PA59&dq=ifs\">page 59</a>,\n</li>\n<li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>1791</b></span> January, “Richardſon’s <i>Chemical Principles of the Metallic Arts</i>”, in <cite>The Monthly Review</cite>, R. Griffiths, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://books.google.com/books?id=F24xcadl9JMC&pg=PA176&dq=ifs\">page <span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\">176</span></a>:</span></div></li>\n<li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><b>2013</b> April 9, Andrei Lankov, “Stay Cool. Call North Korea’s Bluff.”, in <cite>New York Times</cite>‎<sup><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20251107050353/https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/opinion/stay-cool-call-north-koreas-bluff.html?_r=0\">[1]</a></sup>, archived from <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" data-mw-original-href=\"http://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/opinion/stay-cool-call-north-koreas-bluff.html?_r=0\" href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/opinion/stay-cool-call-north-koreas-bluff.html?_r=0\">the original</a> on <span class=\"mw-formatted-date\" title=\"2025-11-07\">7 November 2025</span>:</span></div></li></ul></li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Derived_terms_2\">Derived terms</h4></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Translations_2\">Translations</h4></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Further_reading\">Further reading</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Anagrams\">Anagrams</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"French\">French</h2></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Etymology_2\">Etymology</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Pronunciation_2\">Pronunciation</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Noun_2\">Noun</h3></div>\n<ol><li><a href=\"/wiki/yew\" title=\"yew\">yew</a>\n<ul><li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>1857</b></span>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gustave_Flaubert\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Gustave Flaubert\">Gustave Flaubert</a>, <cite><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madame_Bovary\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Madame Bovary\">Madame Bovary</a><span class=\"q-hellip-sp\">&#160;</span><span class=\"q-hellip-b\"><span style=\"font-style: normal;\">[</span></span><span title=\": Mœurs de province\">…</span><span class=\"q-hellip-b\"><span style=\"font-style: normal;\">]</span></span><span class=\"q-hellip-b\"></span></cite>‎<sup><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14155/pg14155.html\">[2]</a></sup>, Paris: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michel_L%C3%A9vy_Fr%C3%A8res\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Michel Lévy Frères\">Michel Lévy Frères</a>:</span></div></li></ul></li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Further_reading_2\">Further reading</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Japanese\">Japanese</h2></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Etymology_3\">Etymology</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Pronunciation_3\">Pronunciation</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Noun_3\">Noun</h3></div>\n<ol><li>\"<a href=\"/wiki/what-if\" title=\"what-if\">what-if</a>\" <a href=\"/wiki/alternative\" title=\"alternative\">alternative</a> <a href=\"/wiki/history\" title=\"history\">history</a> <span class=\"ib-brac qualifier-brac\">(</span><span class=\"ib-content qualifier-content\">real-life</span><span class=\"ib-brac qualifier-brac\">)</span> / <a href=\"/wiki/event\" title=\"event\">events</a> <span class=\"ib-brac qualifier-brac\">(</span><span class=\"ib-content qualifier-content\">fictional</span><span class=\"ib-brac qualifier-brac\">)</span>\n</li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Synonyms\">Synonyms</h4></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"References\">References</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Middle_English\">Middle English</h2></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Alternative_forms_2\">Alternative forms</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Etymology_4\">Etymology</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Pronunciation_4\">Pronunciation</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Conjunction_2\">Conjunction</h3></div>\n<ol><li><span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\"><a class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" href=\"#English\">if</a></span>, on <a href=\"/wiki/condition\" title=\"condition\">condition</a> that</li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Descendants\">Descendants</h4></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"References_2\">References</h4></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Norman\">Norman</h2></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Etymology_5\">Etymology</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Noun_4\">Noun</h3></div>\n<ol><li><span class=\"usage-label-sense\"><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">(</span><span class=\"ib-content label-content\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/J%C3%A8rriais\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Jèrriais\">Jersey</a></span><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">)</span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/yew\" title=\"yew\">yew</a></li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Old_French\">Old French</h2></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Etymology_6\">Etymology</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Noun_5\">Noun</h3></div>\n<ol><li><a href=\"/wiki/yew\" title=\"yew\">yew</a></li>\n<li>yew wood</li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Descendants_2\">Descendants</h4></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Tarifit\">Tarifit</h2></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Etymology_7\">Etymology</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Pronunciation_5\">Pronunciation</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Verb\">Verb</h3></div>\n<ol><li>to be <a href=\"/wiki/better\" title=\"better\">better</a></li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Conjugation\">Conjugation</h4></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"References_3\">References</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Volapük\"><span id=\"Volap.C3.BCk\"></span>Volapük</h2></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Etymology_8\">Etymology</h3></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Conjunction_3\">Conjunction</h3></div>\n<ol><li><span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\"><a class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" href=\"#English\">if</a></span>\n<ul><li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>1932</b></span>, Arie de Jong, <cite>Leerboek der Wereldtaal</cite>, page <span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\">19</span>:</span></div></li>\n<li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>1952</b></span>, Arie de Jong, <cite>Diatek nulik: Gospul ma ‚Matthaeus’. Kapit: V</cite>:</span></div></li></ul></li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Yola\">Yola</h2></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Conjunction_4\">Conjunction</h3></div>\n<ol><li><span class=\"form-of-definition use-with-mention\">alternative form of <span class=\"form-of-definition-link\"><i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"yol\"><a href=\"/wiki/yith#Yola\" title=\"yith\">yith</a></i></span></span>\n<ul><li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>1867</b></span>, <cite>GLOSSARY OF THE DIALECT OF FORTH AND BARGY</cite>, page <span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\">52</span>:</span></div></li>\n<li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>1867</b></span>, “JAMEEN QOUGEELY EE-PEALTHE”, in <cite>SONGS, ETC. IN THE DIALECT OF FORTH AND BARGY</cite>, page <span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\">110</span>, lines <span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\">5-6</span>:</span></div></li></ul></li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"References_4\">References</h3></div></div>"
